    "goal": "Recapitulate mid-range venular wall shear stress (0.3 Pa / 3 dyn/cm²) in a perfused microfluidic channel.",
    "rationale": "Venular wall shear stress in vivo is typically ~0.1–1 Pa (mid-range ≈ 0.3 Pa). A 400 µm × 100 µm rectangular channel with culture-medium viscosity (1e-3 Pa·s) reaches 0.3 Pa at 12 µL/min per channel (flow_rate_for_shear_stress). This is within the physiological shear range for endothelial cells (HUVEC 0.1–1.0 Pa), making it suitable for a venular endothelium model. Flow is laminar (Re ≈ 0.8) and the pressure drop is modest (~120 Pa), well within syringe-pump capability.",
